          "id": 715542119,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@desowin After moving `delete main_w` after `epan_cleanup()` we now get a crash in `proto_tree_free()` when having `tree_data->interesting_hfids` while closing Wireshark. This happens when doing \"Follow TCP/UDP stream\" and then Quit. Are you able to have a look at this issue before the 3.6.0 release?\n\nStack trace from a recent 3.6.0 build:\n```\n7   libwireshark.15.0.0.dylib     \t       0x1140ed4fd proto_report_dissector_bug + 525 (proto.c:1510)\n8   libwireshark.15.0.0.dylib     \t       0x1140ecef1 free_GPtrArray_value + 177 (proto.c:741)\n9   libglib-2.0.0.dylib           \t       0x107bf5a01 g_hash_table_foreach + 161\n10  libwireshark.15.0.0.dylib     \t       0x1140ed0e1 proto_tree_free + 81 (proto.c:802)\n11  libwireshark.15.0.0.dylib     \t       0x1140c0791 epan_dissect_cleanup + 193 (epan.c:688)\n12  Wireshark                     \t       0x106308748 FrameInformation::~FrameInformation() + 72 (frame_information.cpp:61)\n```",
